  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"In the Syrian regions of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa, the failure of engineered water control—a critical hydraulic overfill in reservoirs—catastrophically re-shaped the landscape. The resulting destructive inundation of inhabited areas swept away a man-made structure, an earthen bridge, before the emergency response fleet could deploy naval craft for human rescue.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.85,\n      \"center\": \"how-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-2\", \"how-3\", \"how-4\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"An unprecedented climatic deluge, one of the heaviest in three decades, pushed the Euphrates past its embankments. The subsequent loss of young life to the waters and the collapse of a man-made structure stand as a stark disaster outcome, the human cost of a system pushed beyond its limits.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.78,\n      \"center\": \"result-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"how-1\", \"result-0\", \"result-2\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"Following widespread property damage across the Syrian regions, the head of state toured the devastation. His executive survey of the affected area coincided with a diplomatic concession from the neighboring country, an interstate agreement to manage the water flow and begin flood mitigation.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.65,\n      \"center\": \"result-5\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"result-1\", \"result-5\", \"result-4\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
